  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.7.1: WebSocket conformance. The Autobahn TestSuite failed 110 of its 301 cases against 2.7.0; none fail now.\n\nEvery failure was a malformed frame accepted and processed as though it were valid, which a well-behaved client never sends and so nothing had noticed. RFC 6455 section 5.2 requires RSV1-3 to be zero unless a negotiated extension defines them, and reserves every opcode outside 0x0-0x2 and 0x8-0xA; both were ignored. Section 5.4 requires a continuation frame to continue something, so an orphan continuation or a data frame arriving mid-fragment is now refused. Section 5.6 requires a text message's payload to be valid UTF-8 and section 8.1 requires the connection to fail with 1007 when it is not; Encoding.UTF8 substitutes U+FFFD and reports success, so invalid input was being echoed back as though it had been understood, which was 75 of the 110 failures. Section 5.5.1 allows a close frame to carry nothing or a two-octet code and an optional reason, and section 7.4.1 reserves the codes; the payload was not read at all and the reply always said 1000 rather than echoing the peer's code.\n\nThis changes what the server accepts. A peer sending invalid UTF-8, setting a reserved bit, or closing with a reserved status code now has its connection failed where it was previously tolerated.",
